@startuml Chrome_Wasm_Render_Engine
!include bluegray.puml
skinparam componentStyle rectangle


title Chrome Browser running NoDOM WASM Render Engine

package "Google Chrome Sandbox" {
    
    component "Browser Window / DOM" as DOM {
        [HTML5 Canvas Element] as Canvas
        [App UI Threads] as JSApp
    }

    package "V8 JavaScript Engine" {
        component "JavaScript Layer" as JSLayer {
            [Engine Wrapper API] as JSWrapper
            [WebGL / Canvas 2D Context] as CanvasCtx
        }
    }

    package "WebAssembly Runtime" {
        component "Wasm Execution Context" as WasmContext {
            [NoDOM Wasm Engine] as WasmCore
            database "Linear Memory\n(SharedArrayBuffer)" as WasmMem
        }
    }
}

' Interactions and Data Flow
JSApp --> JSWrapper : 1. Sends Layout/State Data
JSWrapper --> WasmMem : 2. Writes Input Data (Pointers)
JSWrapper --> WasmCore : 3. Calls nodom.render()

WasmCore --> WasmMem : 4. Processes calculations & updates Framebuffer
WasmCore ..> JSWrapper : 5. Returns execution control

JSWrapper --> CanvasCtx : 6. Reads frame bytes from Wasm Memory
CanvasCtx --> Canvas : 7. Blit/Draw Frame (requestAnimationFrame)

note right of WasmMem
  Holds raw vertex indices,
  textures, and the final pixel
  RGBA color array buffer.
end note

note bottom of WasmCore
  Compiled C++ NoDOM engine.
  Bypasses JS garbage collection
  for constant 60+ FPS rendering.
end note

@enduml
